{
  "why": "SPEC §8B Decisions wire (issue #157): backend openai posts to {baseUrl}/decisions. Questions go as a list in ASCII caller-key order with NO name (keys are addressing, never sent); answers are read back by position. noul -> predicate (criteria folded into instructions), choice -> choices [{value, description?}] in ASCII id order, score -> levels [{label}] in rubric order. Replies normalise to the System One shape (`normalized`, canonical JSON) with calibrated:false; a refusal is an error. Wire shapes recorded from developers.openai.com/api/reference/resources/decisions/methods/create. requestCases: point baseUrl at a capture server, `body` is the exact request bytes, the path is /v1/decisions and no TypeSafe-Danger-Zone-Images header is sent. errorCases fire before any request. captureCases: baseUrl on a local server; every env value is a fake.",
  "questions": {
    "damaged": {
      "type": "noul",
      "instructions": "Does the customer report a damaged item?",
      "criteria": {
        "true": "the item is damaged",
        "false": "the item is fine"
      }
    },
    "team": {
      "type": "choice",
      "instructions": "Which team should handle this?",
      "criteria": {
        "shipping": "lost or late parcels",
        "billing": "refunds and payments",
        "other": ""
      }
    },
    "upset": {
      "type": "score",
      "instructions": "How upset is the customer?",
      "criteria": [
        "calm",
        "annoyed",
        "furious"
      ]
    }
  },
